// The unique NPCs (landmarks-npcs spec 3.2, P8-LM-2): thirty authored characters. The eight mentors of the first hour are placed by the onboarding (place kind "role"); the other twenty-two are put into a
// new world by Sim/People/UniqueNpcs.cs after generation: a keeper at a landmark the region has (landmark.keeper names them back), a wanderer or a rival in a town or village, an advisor at a realm's seat.
// Each has an authored dialogue in dialogue/unique/<id>.jsonc (20 to 50 lines). Attributes are strength, toughness, dexterity, perception, wits. "chance_pm" is the chance a fitting world has them at all.
// "schedule": where they are found by day and by night (landmark = the keeper's post, work, home, church, square or road). "heirloom": weapon or relic, named from the culture's own table (names/artefacts.jsonc).
